---
source: crates/rime-check/tests/corpus.rs
---
warning[R0013] (conservative): `totals` is written to, but never read
--> 18:8: `totals` declared here
    23:3: `totals` is only written to
  = note: every use of `totals` stores a field in it, and the table is never read or passed on, so nothing can see what was stored; Rime cannot tell leftover clutter from a table that was meant to be returned
  = help: delete it and the writes to it, or rename to `_totals` if the binding is deliberate

error[R0601] (conservative): `pair.left` and `pair.right` do not swap
--> 31:2: `pair.left` already holds `pair.right`'s value, so this is a no-op
    30:2: `pair.left` takes `pair.right`'s value here
  = note: after the first assignment both hold `pair.right`'s value; `pair.left`'s original value is lost
  = note: valid Luau — but unless an `__index` or `__newindex` metamethod steps in, the second assignment does nothing, which is almost never what was meant
  = help: swap in one statement: `pair.left, pair.right = pair.right, pair.left`
          pair.left, pair.right = pair.right, pair.left

error[R0608] (conservative): 2 names but 3 values
--> 37:2: the last 1 value is discarded: the call still runs, and every result it returns is dropped
  = note: every value still evaluates; only the results past the name count are dropped
  = note: valid Luau — but a count mismatch with single-value expressions is usually an edit slip
